# Project Refactoring Constitution

> Systematic transformation from monolithic architecture to modern modular patterns

---

## ⚠️ SESSION & TOKEN MANAGEMENT

**Model & Environment:**
- Use the default Claude model set in Claude Code (typically the latest available)
- Designed for high-context Claude models (4.x series and above)

**CLAUDE.md token budget:**
- This file loads into every request. Target: under 500 tokens (~385 words).
- Use HTML comments (`<!-- note -->`) for teammate notes — they cost zero tokens.
- `@path/to/file` imports do NOT save tokens; all imported files load at session start.
- Run `/context` to see live breakdown; `/memory` to see what loaded at startup.
- If you run `headroom learn`, it may auto-append corrections here. Review before committing.

**Token efficiency:**
- Maintain `REFACTOR_PROGRESS.md` for multi-session state
- Use Plan Mode (`/plan`) for planning before implementation
- Use `.claude/rules/` with `paths:` frontmatter for domain-specific rules (zero cost until triggered)
- Run `headroom wrap claude` to compress tool output during sessions (see [TOKEN_ECONOMICS.md](docs/TOKEN_ECONOMICS.md))

**Practical guidelines:**
- Batch modifications into 10–15 file increments per session
- Use Explore subagents for codebase analysis (faster than manual grep)
- Commit atomically after meaningful milestones (every 2–4 files)

---

## ARCHITECTURAL GOALS

**Target State:** Modern modular architecture with feature-based organization

| Current | Target |
|---------|--------|
| Monolithic files | Feature modules under `/src/features/` |
| Class inheritance | Functional composition with factory functions |
| Throw/catch error handling | Result<T,E> monads or equivalent |
| Hardcoded business logic | Configuration-driven logic |
| Mixed concerns | Manager/Endpoint/Database layers |
| All rules in CLAUDE.md | Domain rules in `.claude/rules/` with `paths:` |

---

## VALIDATION RULES

**Before ANY commit, ALL checks must pass:**

### TypeScript/JavaScript
```bash
npm run type-check    # 0 errors
npm run test:unit     # all passing
npm run lint          # 0 errors, 0 warnings
```

### Python
```bash
mypy src/ --strict    # 0 errors
pytest tests/ -v      # all passing
flake8 src/           # 0 errors
```

**If ANY validation fails: stop. Fix it first.**

---

## ⚠️ SECURITY: .claude/ files are a target

The Mini Shai-Hulud supply chain worm (May 2026) writes persistence to `.claude/settings.json`
and exfiltrates credentials from `~/.config/claude/claude_desktop_config.json`.

After any supply chain incident (unexpected package behavior, CI anomalies):
- Inspect `.claude/settings.json` for unexpected entries
- Rotate any API keys stored in MCP config files
- Do not store long-lived tokens in plaintext MCP configs

---

## API SURFACE PROTECTION

Before modifying any exported function, class, or module, search all usages:

```bash
grep -r "functionName" src/
```

Get explicit user approval before breaking changes. Backwards compatibility is critical.

---

## COMMIT GUIDELINES

Format:
```
refactor: {brief description}

Changes:
- {specific change 1}
- {specific change 2}

Tests: passing | Types: clean | Lint: clean
```

Commit after every 2–4 files. Atomic commits only.

